# Balamb Garden, SeeD Academy: "This ability costs {1} less to activate for each other Town you control." On turn 3 Bot1 controls one
# other Town (a Gongaga) so the transformation costs {4}{G}{U}, six mana, and its five Moxen cannot pay it. On turn 5 a second Gongaga
# makes it {3}{G}{U}: the five Moxen pay it exactly, leaving nothing in the pool (CR 601.2f, 118.7). Bot2's own Gongaga is not a Town
# Bot1 controls and reduces nothing, and the colored {G}{U} are never reduced.

[Bot1 Deck]
Balamb Garden, SeeD Academy
Gongaga, Reactor Town
Gongaga, Reactor Town
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Gongaga, Reactor Town
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Balamb Garden, SeeD Academy.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Gongaga, Reactor Town.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Gongaga, Reactor Town.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
! Bot1.Battlefield.Balamb Garden, SeeD Academy.Activate(Ability: Transform; Mana: short)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Gongaga, Reactor Town.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Balamb Garden, SeeD Academy.Activate(Ability: Transform)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Balamb Garden, Airborne.Tapped = true
